This product includes software derived from go-jupyter, developed by the Gene
Ontology Consortium:

    https://github.com/geneontology/go-jupyter

go-jupyter solves the same problem — JupyterHub on EC2 giving each participant a
browser terminal with Claude Code — for agentic biocuration workshops. This
project is an independent re-architecture around disposable, per-cohort
infrastructure.

Measured 2026-09-18: roughly 105 of this project's ~1,870 code lines (about 6%)
are derived from it, and those 105 represent about 1% of that project's source.
None of its Terraform, helper scripts, systemd units or curriculum were used.
The following are the derived parts, and they remain subject to the BSD 3-Clause
License reproduced below:

  student-image/seed-home.sh
      The Claude Code state seeding: the set of `.claude.json` and
      `.claude/settings.json` keys that suppress first-run prompts, and the
      `customApiKeyResponses` technique of pre-approving an injected API key by
      its last 20 characters. Ported from that project's
      `jupyterhub_config.py` pre_spawn_hook.

  student-image/skel/.lab-bashrc
      The welcome-banner-then-launch-Claude shell pattern, with a keypress to
      drop to a plain shell instead. The idea comes from its
      `user-templates/*/.bashrc`; the implementation here was written
      independently and shares no lines. Attributed conservatively.

  hub/jupyterhub_config.py
      The Claude Code environment variable set (CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER,
      DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER, DISABLE_TELEMETRY, DISABLE_NON_ESSENTIAL_MODEL_CALLS)
      and the rationale for each. Four variable names; attributed because the
      knowledge of which ones matter is the contribution.

Several operational decisions also follow findings published in that project's
workshop write-up, including the per-seat disk sizing, the session-hygiene and
tone guidance in the example curricula, and the note that model API spend
dominates infrastructure cost.

The remainder of this project — the container-per-student spawner
configuration, code-based authentication, curriculum system, CloudFormation,
the workshop lifecycle scripts and the test suites — is original work under the
MIT License in LICENSE.

